  "name": "@asynq-family/mcp-server",
  "readme": "# Familia MCP Server\n\n<!-- mcp-name: com.familiaplanner/familia -->\n\nMCP server for using [Familia: family planner](https://familiaplanner.com) (formerly Asynq Family) from MCP-compatible assistants.\n\nThe server lets an authorized assistant read family board context, search plans and tasks, create and edit tasks/plans, work with checklist and photo attachments, and look for free days.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Node.js 20 or newer\n- A Familia MCP token\n\nGenerate an MCP token from Familia before connecting a local MCP client.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSet these environment variables in your MCP client:\n\n```bash\nASYNQ_API_TOKEN=<your-token>\nASYNQ_TIMEZONE=Europe/Prague\n```\n\nOptional environment variables:\n\n```bash\nASYNQ_WEB_LOCALE=cs\nASYNQ_API_BASE_URL=https://api.family.asynq.org\nASYNQ_WEB_BASE_URL=https://familiaplanner.com\n```\n\n## Codex Example\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.familia]\ncommand = \"npx\"\nargs = [\"-y\", \"@asynq-family/mcp-server@latest\"]\n\n[mcp_servers.familia.env]\nASYNQ_API_TOKEN = \"<token>\"\nASYNQ_TIMEZONE = \"Europe/Prague\"\nASYNQ_WEB_LOCALE = \"cs\"\n```\n\n## Claude Code Example\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"familia\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@asynq-family/mcp-server@latest\"],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"ASYNQ_API_TOKEN\": \"<token>\",\n        \"ASYNQ_TIMEZONE\": \"Europe/Prague\",\n        \"ASYNQ_WEB_LOCALE\": \"cs\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Tools\n\n- `familia_list_households` - List accessible households and selected context.\n- `familia_list_household_members` - List household members and user IDs for assignment and participant workflows.\n- `familia_get_day_overview` - Get today, another date, or a narrower time window from the family timeline.\n- `familia_get_today_schedule` - Intent tool for today's agenda, including tasks, plans, calendar events, and overdue summary.\n- `familia_get_tomorrow_schedule` - Intent tool for tomorrow's agenda.\n- `familia_get_next_up` - Return the nearest upcoming items from now.\n- `familia_get_weekly_overview` - Return a multi-day family schedule overview, defaulting to seven days.\n- `familia_get_inbox` - Return items needing attention, currently focused on unfinished past task/plan leftovers.\n- `familia_list_past_due` - Explicit overdue/resty tool for unfinished task/plan items from previous days.\n- `familia_search_items` - Search tasks, plans, and calendar events.\n- `familia_create_task` - Create an agreement-backed task, optionally with a due date, recurring rule, idempotency key, and attached checklist/list.\n- `familia_create_list_task` - Intent tool for creating a new task with an attached checklist/list, optional recurring rule, and optional idempotency key.\n- `familia_create_plan` - Create a plan item, optionally with one-time or recurring schedule, participants, existing linked tasks, new related timed tasks, location, and idempotency key.\n- `familia_update_task` - Update an agreement-backed task.\n- `familia_cancel_task` - Soft-cancel an agreement-backed task without permanently deleting its record.\n- `familia_delete_task` - Permanently delete an agreement-backed task and related task schedules, occurrences, reminders, and attachments.\n- `familia_update_plan` - Update a plan item.\n- `familia_delete_plan` - Delete or cancel a plan item.\n- `familia_batch_write` - Run multiple bounded create/update/cancel/delete task writes one by one from a single MCP call; use `repeatRule`/`rrule` for repeated items and one `create_plan` operation with `relatedTasks` for a main trip/event plus related timed actions.\n- `familia_list_attachments` - List photo and checklist/list attachments for a task or plan.\n- `familia_attach_image` - Attach a JPEG, PNG, or WebP image to a task or plan from a data URL or base64 payload.\n- `familia_create_list_attachment` - Attach a checklist/list to an existing task or plan.\n- `familia_update_list_attachment` - Replace the contents of an existing checklist/list attachment.\n- `familia_delete_attachment` - Delete a photo or checklist/list attachment.\n- `familia_find_free_days` - Find consecutive free days for questions such as \"find 4 free days for a long weekend\".\n\nDay overview tools include `counts.calendarEvents` so assistants can surface linked Google Calendar events alongside Familia tasks and plans. They also include an `overdueSummary` count so questions about today's agenda can mention unfinished items from previous days without flooding the main answer.\n\nImage attachment tools accept either `dataUrl` (`data:image/png;base64,...`) or raw `base64Data` with `mimeType`. The backend enforces the same limits as the app: JPEG, PNG, or WebP up to 4 MB.\n\n## Availability Notes\n\n`familia_find_free_days` uses `blockingPolicy: \"availability\"` by default:\n\n- Hard blockers include calendar events and plan kinds such as `event`, `school`, `activity`, `care`, `travel`, and `holiday`.\n- Soft items such as chores, checklists, birthdays, name days, and ordinary task reminders do not block availability by default.\n\nUse `blockingPolicy: \"strict\"` when you want days with no timeline items at all.\n\n## About Familia\n\nFamilia is the family planner for real life. It's a mobile-first family operations app for shared tasks, plans, responsibilities, and household coordination.\n\n- [Website](https://familiaplanner.com)\n- [Privacy Policy](https://familiaplanner.com/privacy)\n- [MCP endpoint](https://mcp.family.asynq.org/mcp)\n- [How Familia works with MCP-compatible assistants](https://familiaplanner.com/journal/005-asynq-family-mcp-for-ai-assistants)\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
